<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n18273" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀφῆλιξ</span></b> , 
			Ion.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπῆλιξ</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῐκος</span>, ὁ, ἡ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>beyond youth,
				elderly,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνὴρ ἀπηλικέστερος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					3.14
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Mul.</u>
				2.120
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Alciphr.
				1.6
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀφηλικεστάτην</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pherecr.
					206
				</span></i>
			: acc. to <i><span class="en">
				Phryn.
				<u>PS</u>
				p.1
			</span></i>
			<i><span class="en">
				B.
			</span></i>, only in 
				Comp.
			 and 
				Sup.
			; but Posit. in <i><span class="en">
				<u>h.Cer.</u>
				140
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Cratin.
				369
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Phryn.Com.
				67
			</span></i> (who used it of <i>young</i> persons, cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀφηλικεστέραν: νεωτέραν,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>, and so later Aristobul.Jud. ap. <i><span class="en">
				Eus.
				<u>PE</u>
				8.10
			</span></i>). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>minor, infant,</i> in law, <i><span class="en">
				<u>POxy.</u>
				487.5
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
